Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Scraping HTML with BeautifulTureen", "Title"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["BeautifulTureen",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/BeautifulTureen"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " brings BeautifulSoup-style ergonomics to the Wolfram Language. You select \
elements from an imported HTML or XML tree by ",
 StyleBox["pattern",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", compose those patterns with structural ",
 StyleBox["combinators",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", and extract the matched content as raw text, readable text, or a notebook \
ready to export. Every function operates on the static ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLObject",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLObject"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " tree that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Import",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Import"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " produces; there is no live DOM, no CSS engine, and no round-trip out to a \
browser."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tutorial walks the whole workflow on one small HTML document: import \
the tree, find elements with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLPattern",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLPattern"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CSSClass",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/CSSClass"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 ", narrow the search with the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Child",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Child"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Descendant",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Descendant"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Adjacent",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Adjacent"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Sibling",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Sibling"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " combinators, prune unwanted subtrees with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLDeleteCases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLDeleteCases"]],
   "InlineFormula"],
 ", and finally turn what remains into text with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLTextContent",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLTextContent"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLInnerText",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLInnerText"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " or into a document with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLToNotebook",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLToNotebook"]],
   "InlineFormula"],
 "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything starts from the tree that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Import",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Import"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " returns for the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\"\<HTML\>\"", "TR"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["\"\<XMLObject\>\"", "TR"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " format. Import a small HTML fragment to work with throughout, and look at \
what comes back:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["tree=ImportString[\"
<article>
  <h1>Tureen Soup Bar</h1>
  <p class=\\\"lead\\\">Seasonal <b>bowls</b>, made to order.</p>
  <nav class=\\\"menu compact\\\">
    <a href=\\\"/menu\\\">Menu</a>
    <a href=\\\"/hours\\\">Hours</a>
  </nav>
  <ul class=\\\"menu specials\\\">
    <li class=\\\"specials\\\"><a href=\\\"/miso\\\">Miso</a></li>
    <li><a href=\\\"/pho\\\">Pho</a></li>
    <li><a href=\\\"/ramen\\\">Ramen (sold out)</a></li>
  </ul>
  <script>track();</script>
</article>\",{\"HTML\",\"XMLObject\"}];
tree"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"XMLObject", "[", "\"Document\"", "]"}], "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"XMLObject", "[", "\"Declaration\"", "]"}], "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"Version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1.0\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"Standalone\"", "\[Rule]", "\"yes\""}]}], "]"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"article\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/\"", ",", "\"xmlns\""}], "}"}], "\[Rule]", "\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"\\n  \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"h1\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Tureen Soup Bar\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n  \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"p\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"lead\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"Seasonal \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"b\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"bowls\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\", made to order.\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n  \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"nav\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"menu compact\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"\\n    \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"shape\"", "\[Rule]", "\"rect\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"href\"", "\[Rule]", "\"/menu\""}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Menu\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n    \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"shape\"", "\[Rule]", "\"rect\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"href\"", "\[Rule]", "\"/hours\""}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Hours\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n  \""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n  \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"ul\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"menu specials\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"li\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"specials\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"shape\"", "\[Rule]", "\"rect\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"href\"", "\[Rule]", "\"/miso\""}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Miso\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"li\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"shape\"", "\[Rule]", "\"rect\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"href\"", "\[Rule]", "\"/pho\""}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Pho\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"li\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"shape\"", "\[Rule]", "\"rect\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"href\"", "\[Rule]", "\"/ramen\""}]}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"Ramen (sold out)\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n  \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"script\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"track();\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\"\\n\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Wolfram Language has a native representation for HTML, so the page is \
now an ordinary expression you can read. Every tag became an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLElement",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLElement"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["tag", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["attributes", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["children", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 ": a tag name, its attributes as a list of rules, and its contents as a \
list. The contents list holds the text inside the tag and, in place, the \
elements that tag contains, so the nesting of the HTML is the nesting of the \
expression. Wrapping all of it is an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    ButtonBox["XMLObject",
     BaseStyle->"Link",
     ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLObject"], "[", 
    StyleBox["\"\<Document\>\"", "TR"], "]"}], "[", 
   StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]", "TR"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 ", which holds the document's XML declaration alongside the root element."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A few oddities came from the import: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["article", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " has an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["xmlns", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " attribute, the long ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\>\"", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " rule at the head of its attribute list, which names the dialect of the \
markup and says nothing about the page; each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " has an extra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"'", 
    RowBox[{"shape", "'"}]}], " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"'", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "'"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " attribute; and the source's indentation is present as plain strings \
between the elements."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Being an ordinary expression means the standard ",
 ButtonBox["pattern language",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"tutorial/Patterns"],
 " already applies. With nothing but built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Cases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Cases"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " and the three-argument ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLElement",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLElement"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " form, take a census of the tags:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Union", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tag_", ",", "_", ",", "_"}], "]"}], ":>", "tag"}], ",", 
    "Infinity"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", "\"article\"", ",", "\"b\"", ",", "\"h1\"", ",", "\"li\"", ",", "\"nav\"", ",", "\"p\"", ",", "\"script\"", ",", "\"ul\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every tag in that list came from the source. Notice what plain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Cases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Cases"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " made you spell out: the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Infinity",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Infinity"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " level specification, because elements nest arbitrarily deep, and the full \
three-argument ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLElement",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLElement"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["tag", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["_", "TR"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["_", "TR"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " shape."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["BeautifulTureen",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/BeautifulTureen"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " packages exactly this kind of query into a vocabulary that makes the \
common HTML queries concise. Load the paclet:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<MaximilienTirard`BeautifulTureen`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["The same census, now through the paclet's vocabulary:", "Text"],

Cell["XXXX", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {"XXXX", Cell[
    "XXXX", "TableText"]},
   {"XXXX", Cell[
    "XXXX", "TableText"]},
   {"XXXX", Cell[
    "XXXX", "TableText"]}
  }]], "DefinitionBox"],

Cell["XXXX.", "Caption"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["XXXX", "MathCaption"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Union", "[", 
  RowBox[{"XMLCases", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", "tag_", "]"}], ":>", "tag"}]}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:="],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", "\"article\"", ",", "\"b\"", ",", "\"h1\"", ",", "\"li\"", ",", "\"nav\"", ",", "\"p\"", ",", "\"script\"", ",", "\"ul\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Notice ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Cases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Cases"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " became ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLCases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLCases"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLElement",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:ref/XMLElement"], "[", 
   RowBox[{"tag_", ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["_", "TR"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["_", "TR"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " became ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLPattern",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLPattern"], "[",
    "tag_", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 "; and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Infinity",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Infinity"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " is gone. So for simple tasks, not much changes."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Selecting elements", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLPattern",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLPattern"], "[", 
   StyleBox["tag", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " matches any element with the given tag; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["XMLPattern",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLPattern"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["tag", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["constraints", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]", "TR"]}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " adds attribute constraints.  Use a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["RuleDelayed",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/RuleDelayed"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " inside ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLCases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLCases"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " to do transformations on each match, just like you would for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Cases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Cases"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"XMLCases", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<href\>\"", "->", "target_"}]}], "]"}], ":>", "target"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"/menu\"", ",", "\"/hours\"", ",", "\"/miso\"", ",", "\"/pho\"", ",", "\"/ramen\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The constraint expresses that the element must have an ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<\!\(\*StyleBox[\"href\", \"TI\"]\)\>\""], "InlineFormula"],
 " attribute and captures its value as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["target", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " using a named ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Pattern",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Pattern"]], "InlineFormula"],
 "."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "When you want just one element, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLFirstCase",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLFirstCase"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " short-circuits on the first match and returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Missing",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Missing"], "[", 
   StyleBox["\"\<NotFound\>\"", "TR"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " (or a supplied default) when nothing matches. Grab the lead paragraph by \
its class using a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CSSClass",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/CSSClass"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " constraint:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"XMLFirstCase", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
   RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", ",", 
     RowBox[{"CSSClass", "[", "\"\<lead\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"p\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"lead\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"Seasonal \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"b\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"bowls\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\", made to order.\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Even though classes are stored as an element attribute, use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CSSClass",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/CSSClass"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " rather than an attribute constraint to match one:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"XMLFirstCase", "[", 
     RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tag_", ",", "#"}], "]"}], ":>", "tag"}]}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<class\>\"", "->", "\"\<menu\>\""}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"CSSClass", "[", "\"\<menu\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"NotFound\"", "]"}], ",", "\"nav\""}], "}"}]], "Output"],

Cell[TextData[{"The attribute constraint asks for a ", Cell[BoxData["\"\<\!\(\*StyleBox[\"class\", \"TI\"]\)\>\""], "InlineFormula"], " of exactly ", Cell[BoxData["\"\<\!\(\*StyleBox[\"menu\", \"TI\"]\)\>\""], "InlineFormula"], ", but the ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["nav", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"], " carries the string ", Cell[BoxData["\"\<\!\(\*StyleBox[\"menu compact\", \"TI\"]\)\>\""], "InlineFormula"], ": CSS puts every class an element has in that one attribute, separated by spaces. An attribute rule can only match the syntax of the value, its text; ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["CSSClass", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/CSSClass"]], "InlineFormula"], " matches its semantics, the list of classes that text stands for."}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{"One ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["CSSClass", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/CSSClass"]], "InlineFormula"], " can say more than one thing: an ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["Alternatives", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Alternatives"]], "InlineFormula"], " accepts any of several classes, each further argument is another requirement, and ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{ButtonBox["Except", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Except"], "[", StyleBox["cls", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], " rules a class out. A class list is what is being tested, and an element with no ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["class", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"], " attribute has an empty one, so ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{ButtonBox["Except", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Except"], "[", StyleBox["cls", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], " matches such an element too \[LongDash] exactly as CSS ", Cell[BoxData[":not(.cls)"], "InlineFormula"], " does. Ask for the ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["menu", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"], " or ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["specials", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"], " elements that are not ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["compact", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"], ":"}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["XMLCases[tree,XMLPattern[tag_,CSSClass[\"menu\"|\"specials\",Except[\"compact\"]]]:>tag]"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"li\"", ",", "\"ul\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structural combinators", "Section"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A bare pattern ignores where an element sits in the tree. The four \
combinators add that structure, each mirroring a CSS selector: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Child",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Child"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["parent", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["child", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " matches a direct child (CSS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"parent", " ", ">", " ", "child"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 "); ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Descendant",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Descendant"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["ancestor", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["desc", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " matches at any depth (CSS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ancestor", " ", "desc"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 "); ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Adjacent",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Adjacent"], "[", 
   
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["before", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["after", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " matches the element immediately following a sibling (CSS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"before", " ", "+", " ", "after"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 "); and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["Sibling",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Sibling"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["before", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["after", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " matches any following sibling (CSS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"before", " ", "~", " ", "after"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 ")."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "All four are accepted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLCases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLCases"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLFirstCase",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLFirstCase"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Child",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Child"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Descendant",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Descendant"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " are also accepted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["XMLDeleteCases",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLDeleteCases"]],
   "InlineFormula"],
 ". Restrict the link search to the menu list, so that the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["nav", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " links are left out:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"XMLCases", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Descendant", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<ul\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"CSSClass", "[", "\"\<menu\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<href\>\"", "->", "target_"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ":>", 
    "target"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"/miso\"", ",", "\"/pho\"", ",", "\"/ramen\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Adjacent",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Adjacent"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " reaches for content by its position relative to a landmark. Here, the \
landmark is the paragraph that immediately follows the top heading:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"XMLCases", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tree", ",", 
   RowBox[{"Adjacent", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", "\"\<h1\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"XMLPattern", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"p\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"class\"", "\[Rule]", "\"lead\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"Seasonal \"", ",", RowBox[{"XMLElement", "[", RowBox[{"\"b\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", "\"bowls\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\", made to order.\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Pruning the tree", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{"Selection pulls elements ", StyleBox["out", FontSlant->"Italic"], "; ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["XMLDeleteCases", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/XMLDeleteCases"]], "InlineFormula"], " removes them ", StyleBox["in place", FontSlant->"Italic"], ", returning the tree with every match (and its whole subtree) gone. It is the natural first step before reading a document as text: strip the chrome and the non-content tags, then extract. The tag argument takes a pattern, so an ", Cell[BoxData[ButtonBox["Alternatives", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/Alternatives"]], "InlineFormula"], " of tags clears several categories in one pass. Remove the tracking script and the navigation, keeping the surrounding ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{ButtonBox["XMLObject", BaseStyle -> "Link", ButtonData -> "paclet:ref/XMLObject"], "[", StyleBox["\"Document\"", "TR"], "]"}], "[", StyleBox["\[Ellipsis]", "TR"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], " intact:"}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["readable=XMLDeleteCases[tree,XMLPattern[\"script\"|\"nav\"]];XMLCases[readable,XMLPattern[\"a\",\"href\"->target_]:>target]"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"/miso\"", ",", "\"/pho\"", ",", "\"/ramen\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["nav", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " anchors are gone and only the menu links survive. A conditioned pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"pat$", " ", "/;", " ", "test$"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " deletes selectively; names bind as in ordinary pattern matching, and a \
leading name on the whole matched element (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"el$", " ", ":", " ", "pat$"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 ") lets the test call ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["HTMLTextContent",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLTextContent"], "[", 
   StyleBox["el", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " on it. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Adjacent",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Adjacent"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Sibling",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/Sibling"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " combinators are not accepted here, since deletion by relative position is \
ambiguous."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Extracting text", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two functions turn a tree into a string, and the choice between them is the \
same one the web platform draws between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["textContent", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["innerText", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLTextContent",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLTextContent"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " is the lossless concatenation of every descendant string in document \
order. It is faithful but verbose, preserving source whitespace and inserting \
nothing at block boundaries. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLInnerText",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLInnerText"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " renders the tree as it is ",
 StyleBox["meant",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to read: whitespace runs collapse, block-level tags break onto their own \
lines, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["br", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " becomes a newline, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["pre", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " stays verbatim, and non-rendered tags are dropped. Those rules are a \
browser's: the markup keeps every space and newline an author typed, and the \
collapsing happens only at layout, where a run of whitespace comes out as a \
single space and whitespace between two blocks comes out as nothing. This is \
where the indentation strings of the imported tree go. Compare the two on the \
pruned page:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"HTMLTextContent", "[", "readable", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"HTMLInnerText", "[", "readable", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",Expressi\
onUUID->"a219206c-dbf3-451a-a6e1-76ad677a8236"],

Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"\\n  Tureen Soup Bar\\n  Seasonal bowls, made to order.\\n  \\n  MisoPhoRamen (sold out)\\n  \\n\"", ",", "\"Tureen Soup Bar\\nSeasonal bowls, made to order.\\nMiso\\nPho\\nRamen (sold out)\""}], "}"}]], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLInnerText",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLInnerText"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 " classifies each element by tag alone, using a frozen snapshot of the \
default user-agent stylesheet; it never reads a page's CSS. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Roles\>\"", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " option overrides that classification (for example, to skip a \
screenreader-only span), and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<BlockSeparator\>\"", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " sets the string that joins block boundaries."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Converting to a notebook", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "When plain text is too lossy (you want the headings, lists, links, and \
emphasis to survive), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLToNotebook",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLToNotebook"]],
   "InlineFormula"],
 " projects the tree into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Notebook",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Notebook"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " expression. Block tags become cells and inline tags become boxes; from \
that notebook, Markdown, PDF, RTF, and on-screen display all follow through \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Export",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Export"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ". The notebook is the common ancestor of every one of those outputs, which \
is why it, rather than a direct string emitter, is the primitive. Convert the \
pruned page to Markdown:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ExportString", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"HTMLToNotebook", "[", "readable", "]"}], 
   ",", "\"\<Markdown\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["\"# Tureen Soup Bar\\n\\nSeasonal **bowls**, made to order.\\n\\n- [Miso](/miso)\\n\\n- [Pho](/pho)\\n\\n- [Ramen (sold out)](/ramen)\""], "Output"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Headings map to a descending ladder of cell styles, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["li", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " to depth-aware ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Item",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Item"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " styles, and inline ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["code", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " to their Markdown equivalents. Two option layers shape the result: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Roles\>\"", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " re-decides block-versus-inline placement (the layer shared with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["HTMLInnerText",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:MaximilienTirard/BeautifulTureen/ref/HTMLInnerText"]], 
  "InlineFormula"],
 "), while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Constructs\>\"", "TR"]], "InlineFormula"],
 " supplies the concrete form: a cell style, an inline token, or a \
constructor function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["element", "TI"], "\[RuleDelayed]", 
   RowBox[{"Cell", "/", "boxes"}]}]], "InlineFormula"],
 " for anything bespoke. With these six verbs (pattern, combinator, delete, \
two text projections, and the notebook conversion), a page goes from imported \
markup to exactly the shape your computation needs."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

